/* Cosmic Atlas — place data.
 *
 * Loaded on demand, the first time someone opens the Chart section. It is the
 * largest asset in the project (~100 KB) and most visitors never need it, so
 * it does not travel with the page. See ensureCities() in js/11-chart.js.
 *
 * Three globals, in this order:
 *
 *   TZS    237 IANA time zone names          ["Africa/Abidjan", ...]
 *   CTRY   160 country names                 ["Afghanistan", ...]
 *   CITIES 3043 records, each a 5-tuple:
 *
 *          [ name,        String  "Shanghai"
 *            countryIdx,  Number  index into CTRY   -> "China"
 *            lat,         Number  degrees north, negative south   (-90..90)
 *            lon,         Number  degrees east,  negative west  (-180..180)
 *            tzIdx ]      Number  index into TZS    -> "Asia/Shanghai"
 *
 * So CITIES[0] is ["Shanghai", 27, 31.22, 121.46, 165], which reads as
 * Shanghai, China at 31.22°N 121.46°E in Asia/Shanghai.
 *
 * The indices exist because repeating the full country and time zone strings
 * on every row would roughly double the file. Latitude and longitude are the
 * city centre to two decimals — about a kilometre, which is far finer than
 * house cusps need. Time zone rules themselves come from the browser's own
 * IANA database via Intl, not from here; this file only says which zone a
 * place is in.
 */
